  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The pushbutton straddles the breadboard centre gap in columns 10 and 12. Pins 1.l/1.r are in column 10 and pins 2.l/2.r are in column 12. This assumes the two legs of one internal pair sit in the same column, one on each side of the gap.",
   "The catalogue names the bank holding rows a-e 't' and the bank holding rows f-j 'b'. The picture labels the rows the other way round. I used the catalogue names, so the wires go into 't' holes (row c) and the button legs go into 10t.e/12t.e and 10b.f/12b.f.",
   "The black wire goes to the second GND pin on the power header, which I mapped to GND.2.",
   "No external resistor is used. Pin 2 uses the Arduino's internal pull-up (INPUT_PULLUP). The onboard LED on pin 13 is part of the Uno board, so it is not a separate part."
  ]
 },
